James Rising inquired about the relationship between ministries of finance and central banks, alongside other economic decision-makers at the national level. I explained that ministries of finance manage fiscal policy, budgeting, and government spending, while central banks handle monetary policy, interest rates, and financial stability. Their collaboration is vital to prevent economic instability, as misalignments can occur between fiscal and monetary policies. Additionally, I highlighted other economic decision-makers, including economic advisory councils, national statistics agencies, sector-specific authorities, regulatory bodies, and trade ministries, each playing crucial roles in shaping national economic governance. I offered to provide more specifics if needed.
